{"beat": 7, "name": "THE HONEST LIMIT", "text": "What you can do yourself is fit one product's curve in a spreadsheet. Log of units against log of price, the slope is the elasticity, and the spreadsheet gives you the standard error. What you can't do by hand is keep it honest across 24 products every month, with errors that don't trust the noise to be tidy, and check each decision against 4,000 runs of nothing. That part is a model, and a bad model is worse than the few-week test. What you can do today is stop calling a test a win. Ask how wide the answer is. You can build this yourself. If you're doing real volume and want it run with rigor, this is what I do, and I only get paid when it works.", "provider": "library", "words": [{"word": "What", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.209}, {"word": "you", "start": 0.244, "end": 0.313}, {"word": "can", "start": 0.36, "end": 0.476}, {"word": "do", "start": 0.534, "end": 0.615}, {"word": "yourself", "start": 0.685, "end": 1.219}, {"word": "is", "start": 1.544, "end": 1.718}, {"word": "fit", "start": 1.811, "end": 2.055}, {"word": "one", "start": 2.136, "end": 2.38}, {"word": "product's", "start": 2.438, "end": 2.833}, {"word": "curve", "start": 2.879, "end": 3.193}, {"word": "in", "start": 3.228, "end": 3.297}, {"word": "a", "start": 3.332, "end": 3.367}, {"word": "spreadsheet.", "start": 3.402, "end": 4.11}, {"word": "Log", "start": 4.493, "end": 4.725}, {"word": "of", "start": 4.783, "end": 4.841}, {"word": "units", "start": 4.923, "end": 5.178}, {"word": "against", "start": 5.213, "end": 5.515}, {"word": "log", "start": 5.666, "end": 5.909}, {"word": "of", "start": 5.968, "end": 6.026}, {"word": "price,", "start": 6.095, "end": 6.711}, {"word": "the", "start": 6.954, "end": 7.082}, {"word": "slope", "start": 7.163, "end": 7.663}, {"word": "is", "start": 7.709, "end": 7.86}, {"word": "the", "start": 7.918, "end": 7.988}, {"word": "elasticity,", "start": 8.104, "end": 9.125}, {"word": "and", "start": 9.369, "end": 9.52}, {"word": "t